cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Open Microcosm in research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Open Microcosm: a virtual microscope laboratory of real microscopic life"
abstract: >-
  An open-source simulator of real microscopic life as seen through a laboratory microscope
  (water drops, cell cultures and plant preparations). Cells are soft bodies in a low-Reynolds
  Stokes–Brinkman fluid with diffusing chemistry; metabolism, growth, division, feeding and
  behaviour emerge from the simulation, with measured parameters from the literature,
  reproducible runs and data export with provenance.
authors:
  - family-names: Righetti
    given-names: Joaquin
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/Xooter/Open-Microcosm"
keywords:
  - microscopy
  - protists
  - cell biology
  - ecology
  - simulation
  - soft bodies
  - education
